  "body": "What: Let a machine file or post add user code before and after each tool change (for example dust shoe, vacuum, aggregate head unlock and lock). The macro runs at each tool change of the program and shows in the post preview.\n\nWhy: Thermwood nesting adds pre- and post-tool-change macros. Router ATC and aggregate heads need extra words that no generic post knows. Tool changes on aggregate heads are not described in detail in public pages, so keep the macro generic.\n\nSources: https://www.thermwood.com/updates_control_nesting_home.htm\n\nPart of #2395. Changes posted G-code, so effort:high. Machine controller data: #1907, #1918.\n\nDone means: a post with a macro emits it before and after every tool change in a golden test, and an empty macro changes no output.\n",
